-- A `number` receiver's method inside a recursive binding group is
-- `unknown_method` at the use, in every declaration order (checker-v2.md
-- §10.8). `mb` passes the literal `3` for `ma`'s
-- `x`, so `x` is a `number` never chosen between `Int` and `Float`, and
-- nothing can answer `x.size ()`: outside a group the caller reports that
-- (`unknown_method` at the instantiation); inside one, `mb`'s call is a
-- group call and §12.3's case 3 has no structural answer for `size`. It is
-- never an `internal` (at `ma 0 3` or at `x.size ()`) from a wanted left
-- unanswered or an evidence miscount.
ma n x =
    if n > 0 then
        mb n

    else
        x.size ()


mb n =
    ma 0 3
